# Review routing is not the point here — there is one maintainer, and GitHub will
# not ask him to review his own pull request. What this file does is mark the
# paths where a change means more than it looks like, so that an assisted or
# drive-by contribution to one of them is visible as such in the Files tab.
#
# Everything else is deliberately unowned. A list that covers the whole tree
# marks nothing.

# The goldens encode a contract with a build this project no longer keeps a copy
# of, so nothing can re-record them. Changing a recorded value is a decision
# about how the game behaves, not a refactor, and docs/content-provenance.md
# records that the rights position over the derived material is unresolved.
/src/__tests__/goldens/           @williamzujkowski
/src/__tests__/fixtures/goldens/  @williamzujkowski
/src/data/traits.ts               @williamzujkowski

# CI decides what runs against untrusted pull-request content. --ignore-scripts
# lives here, and it is one line from absent.
/.github/workflows/               @williamzujkowski

# The boundary documents themselves. If these drift, every other guard in this
# list is being measured against the wrong statement.
/LICENSE                          @williamzujkowski
/docs/content-provenance.md       @williamzujkowski
/public/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt   @williamzujkowski
